From 614935080b74529a1a6511acfc03ec7197724cc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: forge-shepherd <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 00:46:55 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(shepherd): fix SonarCloud maintainability findings
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Drives new_maintainability_rating back to A on PR #366.

- gatherPullSignal (was CC 20>15): decomposed into a thin orchestrator +
  helpers (safeRead, callIfPresent, gatherFailureExcerpts); hoisted shared
  state defaults. Every optional read now goes through safeRead — NO empty
  catch blocks — and each failure is SURFACED into a new payload `degraded[]`
  ({source,error}) plus the existing `unreadable[]`, instead of being
  swallowed (fixes the "handle or don't catch" smells + tells us WHICH read
  failed).
- runShepherdPass (was CC 20>15, re-flagged as new code after my edits):
  extracted lifecycleOutcome, allRequiredChecksGreen, buildCommentSample, and
  evaluateReviewFeedback so the pass is a thin state-machine dispatch.
- Optional chaining: comment?.author, v.conflicts?.conflicted.
- Math.max(settleRemaining, 0) instead of the ternary.

Behaviour identical — full verdict precedence, fail-closed, review-at-head,
and agnostic-classification suites all still pass (196 tests). Verified
locally with eslint-plugin-sonarjs S3776@15: no function exceeds 15.

Issues: c01936be, 35ee8d78

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
